  "note": "Trace form (research/trace-harness.md) for L07: the twins are a library with no server, so trace/overlay adds a driver (trace-driver.js, one route per function) over the twin's copy; the twins ship no package.json, so trace/package.json names what they import. Every outbound call goes to the harness's stub on 127.0.0.1, which accepts it and never answers; GET /call/orders instead runs the pool's query while another session holds a lock on orders. A request with no response after timeoutMs, longer than every deadline the clean twin sets (5 s at most), in both runs, has no deadline (TMO-01). symbol is the function or client the request drives, for linking to the static finding, which has no endpoint. search() is not driven: it imports search-sdk, a package that does not exist (its static finding is info). defects are what the planted twin must report and the clean twin must not; every other request is a decoy, in both twins. rate and convert wait 25 s: got's timeout.request covers one attempt, and got retries a GET twice after a timeout, waiting about a second between attempts, so a 5 s deadline answers after about 17 s.",
